<title>POLAND: Exbud loses one contract, wins another.</title>
<headline>Exbud loses one contract, wins another.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish construction firm Exbud SA will not carry out the $19.2-million contract agreed last month to build a warehouse for the Czech Republic's Czech-Ogden Airhandling sro, Exbud said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>Exbud said the contract would not be realised at the behest of the Czech firm but gave no other details.</p>
<p>Exbud also said it had won a 7.8-million-zloty tender to build an entrance ramp at a border crossing with Belarus.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
